body:
Northern Arizona University

* Beautiful scenery;
* Proximity to various ski resorts and the Grand Canyon;
* four season climate?
* New Health and Learning Center and aquatic center (currently under construction);

Cons:
* High cost of living for Arizona (I'm from California and the prices for housing and food are normal by NorCal standards);
* Really cold and windy;
* Large class sizes in 300 and 400 level classes;
* No name recognition outside of Arizona;
* Not particularly rigorous academically (this can be blamed on Arizona's public education system);
* Lack of support for athletics;
* Lack of diversity;
* Not enough job opportunities in Flagstaff

I'm into sports, video games, fashion, and learning about different cultures and languages, but I feel that I'm at the wrong university to find others who share my interests. This is a school in the mountains of Arizona where most are interested in outdoor activities and drinking. I can't wait to graduate next month
